12
01:03:16,363 --> 01:03:22,363
The Mule is a 2018 American crime drama film starring and directed by Clint Eastwood, and produced by
Eastwood, Dan Friedkin, Jessica Meier, Tim Moore, Kristina Rivera, and Bradley Thomas.

13
01:08:32,727 --> 01:08:38,727
The screenplay, written by Nick Schenk, is based on the 2014 The New York Times article "The Sinaloa Cartel's 90-Year-Old Drug Mule" by Sam
Dolnick, which recounts the story of Leo Sharp, a World War II  veteran in his 80s who became a drug courier for the Sinaloa Cartel.

14
01:13:49,090 --> 01:13:55,090
The film co-stars Bradley Cooper, Laurence Fishburne,
Michael Peña, Dianne Wiest, and Andy García.

15
01:19:05,454 --> 01:19:11,454
This was Eastwood's first acting project since 2012, and his first
starring leading role in a film directed by himself since 2008.

16
01:24:21,818 --> 01:24:27,818
Filming began in early June 2018, taking place in Atlanta and Augusta,
Georgia, with other film locations in Las Cruces, New Mexico.

17
01:29:38,181 --> 01:29:44,181
The Mule was released in the United States on December 14, 2018, by Warner Bros.

18
01:34:54,545 --> 01:35:00,545
It grossed over $174 million.

19
01:40:10,909 --> 01:40:16,909
The film received generally positive reviews, with critics calling it
"poignant and charming" and praising Eastwood's performance.

20
01:45:27,272 --> 01:45:33,272
The film explores themes of mexico, drug crime,
texas, drug mule, based on true story.

21
01:50:43,636 --> 01:50:49,636
The tone is emotional.
